ion/math-academy-id "q-123173" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,i-({e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,j.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot F=\\text{div}\\,F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-{e}^{x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y). \\\\  & =2{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point  $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2{e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123173/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c18e198-9ea9-57dc-b9af-8c77f0da27cd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123173"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105554/selection/9fc009a21fd1782293e209c8065a326c99bdc4fa3b0b2fa418ce2ae94d2afc70" :answer/id #uuid "5e028754-8cdc-5530-a2ed-b0d7171921cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+2x{cos}^{2}⁡y\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105554/selection/04f2242e3e0bac87423794412aa6966f892e318b6f86dc1b2411c66f41916c37" :answer/id #uuid "72fc8167-9679-5e91-bf33-3b46a5a4dcb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2x{cos}^{2}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105554/selection/051fff8e2280cf2f2974de2809eaf070f4920207da41c185dc690b48a7556237" :answer/id #uuid "b4a45933-3262-