uestion/problem "Consider the vector field $F=xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i+y{x}^{2}\\,j+x{z}^{2}{e}^{y}\\,k.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(1,0,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x{z}^{2}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+{x}^{2}+2xz{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(1,0,-2),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(1,0,-2) & =(-2)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0+{1}^{2}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =-2+1-4 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-131178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6b79409-5a5b-533b-8d46-4e0e6d963b3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "e3e7d861-b673-5495-82f3-7f15e2d39e62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "212fb310-4faf-5d64-b994-9189483d6045" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8239e7a5-edd1-5b1b-8f1c-191d871fac25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8e57c5c9-431e-58e8-975a-82dc89dbc39c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "4c7ea5d8-7af4-54d4-957c-88185d35358c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb201544-8fe8-5b4a-a9a6-9189aae69dab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105578/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-105578/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-105578/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-105578/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-105578/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-105578/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105578" :question/id #uuid "20ed7f14-e721-5bea-bf3a-62dbb2c9f72a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105578" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/33f0353e3856fb2b458d17ed1959918e6a3dd96fd0a966d971575ffc212402f0.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move horizontally and vertically away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection/c878bcdb91a0a5248ccd2809513b6e178833edd108ada4349638294858cbf7f2" :answer/id #uuid "1c67e96a-4075-51aa-a4a4-285e4aafd781" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "38a42ddf-3b9c-595c-8855-147e41853c56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "072b8fa7-7a63-52b1-ad3f-b7866ff1716b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "4d896d77-0832-52b2-a1cb-ce83c1a04008" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "dea9a11b-ae8f-5377-8305-ba7209408238" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "daf39be3-9ec0-5300-8165-7498253bc37b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123245/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-123245/selection/c878bcdb91a0a5248ccd2809513b6e178833edd108ada4349638294858cbf7f2" "q-123245/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-123245/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-123245/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-123245/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123245" :question/id #uuid "38018921-9990-5dba-9670-bdc0a09e028a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123245" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/b315be9ba524ab538388fdaad31161c280d7d6e5ab71261345063ac6ffe819d5.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vectors increase as we move vertically and horizontally away from the origin. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123245/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123245"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "dd2d64c0-3639-5996-86f5-947a1a4473a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "b0461412-de8f-5fe2-9141-f6886e40da78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "978e94a7-ae76-5eb8-98ff-b8647bb760c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "079957cc-8054-54dd-94eb-889c77dca278" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "df52de77-62b9-5d17-8316-bb93ad1fbe12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34167edc-4fd7-5477-8a51-7ce036e0e7e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105575/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer-field/choices ["q-105575/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-105575/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-105575/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-105575/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-105575/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105575" :question/id #uuid "0441cea9-5f0e-50b3-ba06-61f26c6ce00c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105575" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/11d38951b884f17616a61403d793322d0e2ea28910e806fe8f018251508352a1.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044029/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105575/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105046/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e76daccb-a0ec-5854-b291-72550aa50b3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105046/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "ce719098-e4f9-5bf1-98ce-d0880df0d727" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105046/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "bdcf832a-c5cf-5a0d-81ec-755f02dbf018" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105046/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "598ad009-aff7-5434-bc53-d14e9c323c16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105046/